477
00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:12.010
But so, Jenna, here's the thing.

478
00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:14.790
Prima Nocta was a myth.

479
00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:19.610
There's actually no historical evidence that this ever happened.

480
00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:22.310
According to the Internet, this was just something that was literary.

481
00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:28.470
And I did a deep dive on Reddit, guys, and I-D-J-E-T, that's the handle.

482
00:21:28.690 --> 00:21:29.710
They wrote this.

483
00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:33.790
Prima Noctus did not exist as any feudal right or custom.

484
00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:39.150
There are a handful of mentions of it in medieval sources, but they're all literary,

485
00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.050
not historical.

486
00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:42.910
It's a myth that developed after the Middle Ages.

487
00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:49.330
In 19th century, French historians interested in creating a negative portrayal of the Dark

488
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:55.510
Ages for their own political reasons, created a custom out of it and gave it a Latin name,

489
00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.010
thus making it real.

490
00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:03.270
The actual history of the development of the idea of Prima Noctus is way more fascinating

491
00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:11.050
than the idea itself because it tells us a lot about how historians bring biases to their

492
00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:12.430
sources and opinions.

493
00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:14.230
I found that fascinating.

494
00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:17.810
Who writes the history, writes the history.

495
00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:23.050
Yes, this is why women and people of color are missing from the history books.

496
00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:25.090
It's not that we weren't contributing, y'all.

497
00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:27.390
It's that we didn't get to write it down.

498
00:22:27.770 --> 00:22:28.210
Right.

499
00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:30.390
Someone else wrote it down.

